      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/ac8455/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-28T16:20:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Okay, so in our last game I was playing Visionary agains Omnitron and threw Wrest the Mind on an Electro-Pulse Explosive. My party agued that it couldn’t be done… I cited that Wrest says “Play next to a target” and that “any card with hp is a target”. So it should have been a legal play, right?</p>\n<p>Now, we went around the table when Electro activated and I shifted its 15 over to a second Electro which was also in play, offing it, dealt the Electro that the Wrest was on 2 dmg and Visionary her two, then moved to the next hero, shifted the 13 it was currently at to Omnitron himself, 2 to Electro then Visionary, etc… Leaving Electro at 5 hp, Visionary at 16 and Omnitron at 60.</p>\n<p>Does that all wash, or did I munchkin it up a bit?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:43.225Z",
